%description:

A deviation of StochasticChannelModel from the specification, pinned and not
endorsed: the LOS state of an indoor UE's link is drawn against the LOS
probability at the link's whole 2D distance, where the table takes the outdoor
part of it.

TR 38.901 v16.1.0 Table 7.4.2-1 ("LOS probability"), row UMa: "Pr_LOS = 1,
d2D-out <= 18m", and for "18m < d2D-out" a function of d2D-out alone (and of
h_UT); the rows RMa and UMi - Street canyon are functions of d2D-out likewise.
Figure 7.4.1-2 ("Definition of d2D-out, d2D-in and d3D-out, d3D-in for indoor
UTs") has d2D = d2D-out + d2D-in. The model passes the strategy the link's d2D.

Checked on a UMa cell, on fifty indoor UEs 40 m from the base station on the
ground and 25 m inside their building, so d2D-out = 15 m. Each link's first
evaluation draws its LOS state; the draw is replayed from a copy of the model's
generator. Every state is the draw against the probability at d2D = 40 m,
0.7415, and so some of the links are NLOS; at d2D-out = 15 m the table's
probability is 1. ChannelModelIndoorLineOfSightSpec asserts the specification as
an expected failure. When the model follows it, change this test together with
that one.

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        channelModel: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

# the LOS state is drawn; the first number a link's first evaluation draws is its
**.dynamicLos = true
**.shadowing = false
**.fading = false

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *model = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "channelModel");
auto *medium = harnessModule<CellularRadioMedium>(this, "radioMedium");
ChannelModelProbe probe(model);

// a UMa base station, and fifty indoor UEs at one place: 40 m from it on the
// ground, 25 m inside their building, so 15 m of the 40 are outdoors
const int numUes = 50;
const double d2D = 40.0, d2DIn = 25.0;
StubEndpoint bs;
bs.nodeId = MacNodeId(1);
bs.coord = Coord(0, 0, 25);
StubRadioRegistration bsRadio(medium, bs.nodeId, &bs);
std::vector<std::unique_ptr<StubEndpoint>> ues;
std::vector<std::unique_ptr<StubRadioRegistration>> ueRadios;
for (int i = 0; i < numUes; i++) {
    ues.push_back(std::make_unique<StubEndpoint>());
    ues[i]->nodeId = MacNodeId(1025 + i);
    ues[i]->coord = Coord(d2D, 0, 1.5);
    ues[i]->insideBuilding = true;
    ues[i]->insideDistance = d2DIn;
    ueRadios.push_back(std::make_unique<StubRadioRegistration>(medium, ues[i]->nodeId, ues[i].get()));
}
const double d3D = bs.coord.distance(ues[0]->coord);
// the strategy's LOS probability at the whole 2D distance, and at its outdoor part
const double pAtD2D = probe.pathLoss()->computeLosProbability(probe.deployment(25, 1.5), d3D, d2D);
const double pAtD2DOut = probe.pathLoss()->computeLosProbability(probe.deployment(25, 1.5), d3D, d2D - d2DIn);

wait(0.010);

// The first evaluation of each UE's downlink draws its LOS state; the draw is
// replayed from a copy of the model's generator.
int numLos = 0, numAsAtD2D = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < numUes; i++) {
    RadioLink link = probe.whatIfLink(ues[i].get(), dlCqiTransmission(&bs, ues[i]->nodeId));
    RngSnapshot snapshot(model);
    model->getAttenuation(link);
    bool los = probe.losMap().at(link.stateKey()).los;
    double u = omnetpp::uniform(snapshot.rng(), 0.0, 1.0);
    numLos += los;
    numAsAtD2D += (los == (u <= pAtD2D));
}

c.expectNear("the strategy's LOS probability at d2D = 40 m, for a 1.5 m UT", pAtD2D, 18.0 / 40 + std::exp(-40.0 / 63) * (1 - 18.0 / 40), 1e-12);
c.expectNear("...and at d2D-out = 15 m", pAtD2DOut, 1.0, 0);
c.expectValue("PINNED DEFECT: an indoor UE's LOS state is its draw against the probability at d2D, for every one of the links", numAsAtD2D, numUes);
c.check("PINNED DEFECT: ...so some of the links are NLOS, 15 m outdoors from the base station", numLos < numUes, std::to_string(numLos) + " of " + std::to_string(numUes) + " in LOS");

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=4 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
